      "text": "To find the median room number of the other 19 Mathletes, we need to first determine the median of the room numbers 1 through 21, excluding the rooms 12 and 13. The median of a set of numbers is the middle number when the set is arranged in ascending order.\n\nHere are the steps to solve the problem:\n\n1. List the room numbers from 1 to 21.\n2. Exclude the rooms 12 and 13.\n3. Sort the remaining room numbers.\n4. Find the median of the sorted list.\n\nLet's write the Python code to perform these steps.\n```python\n# List of room numbers from 1 to 21\nroom_numbers = list(range(1, 22))\n\n# Exclude rooms 12 and 13\nroom_numbers = [room for room in room_numbers if room not in [12, 13]]\n\n# Sort the remaining room numbers\nroom_numbers.sort()\n\n# Find the median\nn = len(room_numbers)\nmedian = room_numbers[n // 2] if n % 2 != 0 else (room_numbers[n // 2 - 1] + room_numbers[n // 2]) / 2\n\nprint(median)\n```\n```output\n11.0\n```\nThe median room number of the other 19 Mathletes, excluding the rooms 12 and 13, is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).",
